      "side": 1,
      "message": "My initial patch set tried to fix the issue by calling host_set_single_event(EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE) in motion_lid_set_dptf_profile.\nSo this case is exactly what I want to fix - notify AP to update DPTF when the device enters flipped-360 mode (please see the commit message for more details).\n\nThere are two paths of flipped-360 mode detection: (1) GMR sensor (2) Lid accel (motion_lid).\nFor now, both paths fail to notify AP for DPTF update.\nCalling host_set_single_event(EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE) in acpi_dptf_set_profile_num() can fix both paths.\nAlternatively, we can go back to the initial patch sets of this CL and CL:1747061.\n\nFor the other callers of acpi_dptf_set_profile_num(), they also call tablet_set_mode(), which calls host_set_single_event(EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE), so the current patch is a no-op to them.",
